<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Diego Portales</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1793–1837</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Diego Portales was a Chilean merchant and minister who dominated the conservative governments of the 1830s. He imposed order on a divided country and shaped the centralist Constitution of 1833, which created a strong presidency. Seeing the Peru-Bolivian Confederation as a threat to Chile, he pressed for war against it in 1836, and he was murdered by mutinous troops near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valparaiso">Valparaíso</a> in 1837.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/diego-portales.jpg" alt="Diego Portales" width="320" height="396" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Camilo Domeniconi · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:DPortales.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
